I'm running a small BBS on my XT using a modified TELIX (that's my com
program) host script, and I would like to add an online Nethack
option.  Is there anyone out there who would be willing to help me?

I've made several (increasingly promising) attempts at this, but I'm
still having some problems.

If you have no interest, type 'n' now.  However, I can use all the
help I can get, so I'd appreciate you at least reading this...


At the moment, when you choos the nethack option, TELIX packs up and
exits to dos with %errorlevel=1.

This is picked up by the batch file that runs the BBS, which then
executes whatever instructions are needed.  The problem is that the
caller sees "who are you?", but when they type in thier name, the
characters echo back as junk, and nothing else happens - the system
has effectivly crashed.

I've turned off rawio in Nethack.cnf, but that didn't seem to help. 

Here's the part BBS batch file that runs nethack, as it stands at the moment:

:hack
c:\utils\cruise/X                       Uninstall TSR to save space
cd c:\games\nethack
copy nethack.cnf nethack.bk!            Swap configuration files...
copy nethack.bbs nethack.cnf
echo DOS: Playing Nethack
ctty com1:
c:\utils\fixcom                         See below
nethack
ctty con
copy nethack.bk! nethack.cnf            Swap back config files...
cd c:\telix
echo DOS: Hanging up after Nethack
telix o shangup                         Run telix hangup script (custom)
c:\utils\cruise/B/0                     Re-install TSR

Note 1: the utility fixcom does two things: it changes the base
address of com1 in ram to the base address of com3, so that I can CTTY
to my modem.  This is already done in my autoexec by an earlier
version of the program, and works fine for the dos shell function
(which has a custom batch file as well).  The second thing this
program does, and this is upon the advice of a friend who knew a
little more about what was going on than I did) is to set the fourth
byte of the serial controll ports to 0x0B, or 00001011.  I'm not sure
what the point of this is, but whithout it you don't even see "who are
you" - the system just crashes.

*Any* help would be appreciated.

